turnkey-fileserver-19.0 (1) turnkey; urgency=low

  * Fix firewall port conf: appended FTP port (21) was discarded by the port
    assignment in fileserver.mk; use += so it survives.

  * Reload smbd instead of the non-existent 'samba' service in the
    samba-sudoadmin firstboot hook.

  * smb.conf: drop deprecated 'socket options' and the no-op 'os level'.

  * Drop WINS support & document network discovery (wsdd + avahi) and how to
    re-enable WINS if required in the new  /etc/samba/README-discovery.txt.

  * Disable legacy NetBIOS: serve SMB on port 445 only, disable nmbd, and
    close the NetBIOS firewall ports (139/tcp, 137-138/udp). As noted above
    discovery is handled by wsdd and avahi.

  * Stop opening unused MSRPC port 135 (only served by Samba as an AD DC).

  * Disable the [cdrom] share by default (commented out and documented); it
    only works on hardware with an optical drive and an fstab entry.

 -- Jeremy Davis <jeremy@turnkeylinux.org>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 17:30:12 +1000

turnkey-fileserver-18.0 (1) turnkey; urgency=low

  * Add wsdd package for Windows Service for Devices - so Fileserver shows up
    in Win10/11 Explorer - closes #1598.

  * Install avahi-daemon by default. Provides zeroconf auto network discovery
    and is ompatible with Apple's Bonjour service.

 -- Jeremy Davis <jeremy@turnkeylinux.org>  Thu, 06 Jun 2024 07:42:44 +0000
